<p>Hungary&#x27;s election winner, Péter Magyar, is moving quickly to define the country&#x27;s post-Orbán direction after defeating Viktor Orbán&#x27;s Fidesz party and securing a two-thirds parliamentary majority, according to multiple reports. That margin gives Magyar the power to start undoing changes made during Orbán&#x27;s 16 years in office, with reform of state institutions and renewed ties with the European Union at the center of the transition. Access to frozen EU funds is one of the new government&#x27;s most immediate practical challenges as it tries to convince Brussels that Hungary is serious about tackling corruption and restoring democratic checks. Magyar has also signaled a sharp foreign-policy shift. He said Hungary would stop the outgoing government&#x27;s withdrawal from the International Criminal Court and would be obliged to detain anyone sought by the court who enters the country, a statement that explicitly applies to Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu if he visits. Taken together, the moves point to a broad reset: a more pro-EU and pro-NATO posture, a likely turnover of Orbán-era officials in Brussels, and a stronger emphasis on legal obligations and institutional rebuilding after a high-turnout election that opened a new political chapter for Hungary.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/hzDrYLBCGsyvytw4h36xQiPFoESGP48o4EGIKi-chXEnLLEP68v094CLf8i4pdQnsN_LTz8Gdq6pfBE3tA6gTqTzQZJI_UiN4CDArvK_f5au' alt='Election winner and leader of Hungary’s TISZA party Peter Magyar leaves after a press conference following the first official meeting of TISZA’s new parliamentary group at the HUNGEXPO Congress and Exhibition Center in Budapest, Hungary, on April 20, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>EU envoy: Hungary&#x27;s ambassador to the EU, Bálint Ódor, may lose his post as Magyar prepares to remove figures closely tied to the previous government and recast Budapest&#x27;s approach in Brussels.</li><li>Record turnout: Voter turnout hit a record 80%, underscoring the strength of public participation in an election that produced a decisive mandate for political change.</li><li>ICC reversal: Magyar said his government can stop Hungary&#x27;s ICC withdrawal before it takes effect on June 2, preserving the country&#x27;s treaty obligations.</li><li>Anniversary diplomacy: Magyar said he invited foreign leaders, including Netanyahu, in connection with the 70th anniversary of Hungary&#x27;s 1956 anti-Soviet uprising, which falls later this year.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Péter Magyar: The incoming prime minister says Hungary should reverse its withdrawal from the ICC, comply with court warrants, rebuild relations with the EU and NATO, and restore checks and balances at home. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1993610/hungary-will-carry-out-icc-warrant-against-netanyahu-says-magyar'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Viktor Orbán&#x27;s outgoing administration: Orbán&#x27;s government withdrew Hungary from the ICC after Netanyahu&#x27;s Budapest visit and spent years taking a confrontational line with EU institutions while billions in EU funds were frozen over concerns about democratic freedoms. (<a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/viktor-orban-eu-ambassador-fixer-hungary-fall-guy-balint-odor/'>Politico Europe</a>)</li><li>European policy observers: Former UK ambassador Ivan Rogers said national envoys in Brussels are expected to be loyal to their political leaders and carry out instructions, framing Ódor&#x27;s likely departure as a standard political turnover after a change of government. (<a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/viktor-orban-eu-ambassador-fixer-hungary-fall-guy-balint-odor/'>Politico Europe</a>)</li><li>The Trump administration: Vice President JD Vance publicly supported Orbán before the election, showing how closely Hungary&#x27;s vote was watched beyond Europe. (<a href='https://theweek.com/world-news/maga-takes-hit-hungary-votes-out-orban'>The Week</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.csmonitor.com/World/Europe/2026/0420/peter-magyar-reform-corruption-viktor-orban-fidesz-tisza'>Péter Magyar’s goal now is to reform Orbán’s Hungary. EU funds are at stake.</a> - csmonitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/viktor-orban-eu-ambassador-fixer-hungary-fall-guy-balint-odor/'>Orbán’s EU fixer faces becoming Hungary’s ‘fall guy’</a> - politico.eu</li><li><a href='https://theweek.com/world-news/maga-takes-hit-hungary-votes-out-orban'>MAGA takes a hit as Hungary’s Orban voted out</a> - theweek.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/video/newsfeed/2026/4/20/hungarys-incoming-pm-says-netanyahu-would-be-arrested-if-he-visits'>Hungary’s incoming PM says Netanyahu would be arrested if he visits</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.reddit.com/r/worldnews/comments/1sr999f/hungary_must_arrest_netanyahu_if_he_visits_magyar/'>Hungary must arrest Netanyahu if he visits, Magyar says</a> - reddit.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1993610/hungary-will-carry-out-icc-warrant-against-netanyahu-says-magyar'>Hungary will carry out ICC warrant against Netanyahu, says Magyar</a> - dawn.com</li></ul>